From 50061cf835c58c4345902bd511a18c670c14ce7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:01:40 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Seed: keep the untrimmed base with each kernel and never
 inherit a trim

A plan seeded from "the running kernel" on top of a Kernelsmith build
inherited that build's trimmed config, so every driver dropped earlier
stayed dropped whatever keep families were ticked (a second-generation
build on a Z790 box kept 0 of the 52 USB-serial and 5 of the 314 hwmon
modules the distribution config has).

- plan::resolve_seed: when the running kernel's config carries the
  "-ks-" LOCALVERSION, start from <tree>/.kernelsmith/seed.config (the
  untrimmed base that build began with), else from the newest untrimmed
  seed.config of any earlier job, else warn. File and tree seeds that are
  themselves Kernelsmith configs are flagged too.
- The build script copies the job's seed into the tree only when it is
  untrimmed, so the stored base stays untrimmed across generations.
- kernelsmith plan/build --seed FILE | running | tree | defconfig.
- The Review step shows the resolved base; check() carries the note/warning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
